{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And I will remember My covenant with Jacob.</b> Scripture enumerates here the names of the patriarchs in reverse order. By way of the plain sense (peshat), the reason it put Jacob first is to say: Jacob the younger is worthy enough for this; and if he is not worthy enough, Isaac is with him; and if Isaac is not worthy enough, Abraham is with him. And the term 'remembering' is stated for both of them [Abraham and Jacob], but for Isaac 'remembering' is not stated, because his ashes are gathered upon the altar." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: the word את is stated for Abraham and for Isaac even though Ishmael and Esau issued from them, but for Jacob את is not stated of him even though his bed was complete [all his children were righteous]. From the patriarchs I learn it, but the matriarchs — from where do I learn it? Scripture says: את, את — and there is no את except the matriarchs, as it says (Genesis 49): שמה קברו את אברהם ואת שרה אשתו — there they buried Abraham and Sarah his wife; שמה קברו את יצחק ואת רבקה אשתו — there they buried Isaac and Rebekah his wife; ושמה קברתי את לאה — and there I buried Leah. And so did they expound in Torat Kohanim." "<b>And according to</b> my own opinion, the reason he used the language of אף ('also') for Abraham and Isaac — even though the word אף alludes to the attribute of justice, as in the language of (Genesis 18:25) האף תספה צדיק עם רשע — 'Will You also sweep away the righteous with the wicked?' — is that the attribute of justice was mentioned for the two of them because they were equal in it in the matter of the binding [akedah]: this one mastering his inclination to slaughter his son, and that one mastering his inclination to be slaughtered. And from this Scripture said of them (Genesis 22): וילכו שניהם יחדו — 'and the two of them walked together,' that is, with one intention. And the fact that יעקוב is written plene with a ו״ו: we find in five places that יעקוב is written plene, and in five places אליה is written defective, and our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: Jacob took one letter from the name of Elijah as a pledge, until he comes and brings glad tidings to his children." "<b>And furthermore</b> in the Midrash: Why did he mention the merit of the land together with them? Resh Lakish said: a parable — to a king who had three daughters and one maidservant who raised them. Whenever he inquires after the welfare of the daughters, he says: 'Inquire for me after the welfare of the one who raised them.' End. And he called the three attributes of the patriarchs by the name 'daughters.'" "<b>By way of the Kabbalah:</b> וזכרתי את בריתי יעקב — he put Jacob before the other patriarchs in order to give precedence to זכר, which is mercy, and to arrange the sefirot from below upward. And he specified the sefirot, which are seven: Jacob includes with him the two pillars of heaven, and the middle line, which is alluded to in the added ו״ו of יעקוב; and Isaac, and Abraham, and the land — behold these are seven. And this is the language of בריתי יעקב בריתי — 'My covenant Jacob, My covenant,' that is, he is Jacob [in himself a covenant]; and likewise in all of them: בריתי יצחק בריתי אברהם. And he called each and every one of the supernal patriarchs 'a covenant,' because all of them are included in the covenant; and the land, which is the Nukvah, included from them — I will remember as well. And this very order Scripture adopted where it says (Deuteronomy 4) ויוציאך בפניו בכחו הגדול ממצרים: בפניו — this is Jacob, as it says (Psalms 24) מבקשי פניך יעקב סלה; בכחו — this is Isaac; הגדול — this is Abraham. And further he put Jacob first, so that the Glory gazes upon the form engraved in the Hayyot of the Chariot and has compassion upon Israel." "<b>And what</b> is written: יעקוב — full with ו״ו — alludes to the sixth sefirah, which is his attribute, and it is the ו״ו of the great Name. Beyond this, there is in the word יעקוב when it is full with ו״ו an awakening and an allusion, for in the י״ו of the four-faced living creature (חיה המרובעת) the face of Jacob is fixed. From here you will understand (Numbers 28:14): ״רביעית יין לכבש״ — a quarter-hin of wine for the lamb — but not so for the bull, rather half the hin, and for the ram a third of the hin; and regarding him too, Ezekiel, of blessed memory, mentioned (Ezekiel 1:8): ״ולאדם ידיהם מתחת כנפיהם״ — the letters at the end of the words spell ת״ם, to allude to him: ״ואיש תם״ — and Jacob was a תם, a whole man; and from this it is said: ״יושב אהלים״ — dwelling in tents — and it is as though it said: dwelling on the throne; and furthermore, אהלים — tents — of below and of above, and I have already mentioned this in the section of Toledot Yitzhak. And it was necessary to say ״והארץ אזכור״ — and I will remember the land — in order to mention the Chariot in its completeness, for a chariot is not less than four." "<b>And know</b> the opinion of the Ramban on the secret of the verse: that יעקב is the specific Name that speaks, and therefore יעקוב is full with ו״ו; and therefore it says ״וזכרתי״ — and I will remember — that is to say, I will draw the efflux of emanation from above and bestow it upon the supernal fathers, and the land, which is included in all of them, I will bring to remembrance as well, and then I will have compassion upon Israel — and behold, the entire structure is complete." "<b>And the Midrash</b> called this earth by the name מגדלת in relation to the attributes (middot) that are above it, and they came to allude that the fathers mentioned by the verse — the intention is not concerning those above, and they are called ברית (covenant) because all of them are included in the land called ברית, as I have mentioned."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:18.261630790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}